<title>JAPAN: Sony Music fails to renew contract with pop group.</title>
<headline>Sony Music fails to renew contract with pop group.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sony Music Entertainment (Japan) Inc said  on Friday it will no longer release new recordings of the popular  Japanese pop group Dreams Come True.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that it and the group's music production  company had failed to agree on a new contract.</p>
<p>Dreams Come True has sold more than 22 million albums through company  since its debut in March 1989, a company spokesman said.</p>
</text>
